# Everything in this repo runs on Linux (container) as well as the host.
# Keep LF in the working tree on every OS — a CRLF shebang breaks in the
# container with a misleading "bad interpreter" error.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jar binary
# A release is the exact bytes that were ordered and hashed in its
# MANIFEST.sha256. No end-of-line conversion, in either direction: the JLC
# CSVs are CRLF, and normalising them broke every hash on a fresh clone.
**/release/** -text
